// Heads of items that the parser reads on after one error (W5-11 U4, §18.1, S-492, S-593, S-477):
// an `rt` before a declaration that is not a function, an attribute after a visibility or after
// `rt`, and an `extern` head that cannot be read before its `{`. Whatever the recovery does with
// the text of the head and with what follows, the round trip of the CST gives the file back byte
// for byte (R-86). An input of the CST round trip; fmt refuses it (syntax diagnostics), as it
// must. The forms that are not read on (the ones that do not close, the ones a line break cuts)
// are at the end.

